-# Tests that legitimately read a comment.
-#
-# TestNoTestIsSatisfiedByAComment runs the whole package against a copy with
-# every whole-line comment stripped out of the YAML it reads, and requires
-# every test that passed to still pass. A test that flips was being satisfied
-# by prose - which has happened twice here, most recently a tripwire check
-# satisfied by the comment ABOVE the step it was meant to be asserting.
-#
-# An entry here is an exemption, so it costs what an exemption costs: a reason
-# somebody can read later.
-comment_dependent:
-  - test: TestEveryProofStillFindsItsPlace
-    reason: >
-      Its subject is where each proof's find lands in the file as written,
-      which is the text the ledger applies the mutation to. A find may take in
-      the comment beside the code it breaks, and with the comments stripped
-      such a find has nowhere to land. That moves the anchor, not the guard's
-      verdict on any code.
-  - test: TestEverySilencedFindingNamesTheGuardThatProvesItMayBe
-    reason: >
-      The comment is its subject. A tool's own configuration cannot carry a
-      reason anywhere else, so the guard a silenced entry names is written in
-      the comment above that entry, and a copy with the comments stripped is
-      a copy in which every such entry names nothing.
